{
 "_comment": [
  "Parity corpus for the demographics parser. Every patient is invented.",
  "",
  "The parser runs in two languages now: backend/demographics.py, and",
  "extension/privacy/parse.js, which is what keeps the raw note in the browser.",
  "Both read THIS file and both must reproduce `expect` exactly. Neither",
  "generates it — an expectation a parser writes for itself asserts nothing.",
  "",
  "WHY A PARSER NEEDS A PARITY CORPUS AT ALL, when a missed value only leaves a",
  "blank: the values this finds are the dictionary the note is redacted",
  "against. A name the browser's copy fails to find is a name the redactor is",
  "never told to remove. The failure is one step removed from the leak, which",
  "is exactly what makes it easy to miss in review.",
  "",
  "Each case is chosen for a rule rather than for coverage. Adding one means",
  "naming the rule it pins in its id."
 ],
